`weak` outside a class's own field or a variable is not implemented yet (#3119)
`weak` to anything but a class instance is not implemented yet (#3119)
a `weak` reference reads `null` once its target is gone: its type must include `null`
`weak` refers to an object with an identity: `f64` is not a class, an object type, an interface, an array or a map
`weak` may only be united with `null` (and `undefined`): write `weak T | null`
`weak` is allowed only at the top of the type of a field or a variable (`let`, `const` or `var`: `parent: weak Node | null`)
`weak` refers to an object with an identity: `Pt` is stored by value (a struct, or an interface of fields only)
